---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../../lib/i18n";
---

<Base lang="en" altPath="/terms" title="Terms of Service — Promethena">
  <article class="legal prose">
    <a class="back" href="/en/">← Back to dock</a>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 2026-08-10</p>

    <h2>1. Purpose</h2>
    <p>
      These terms govern the use of Promethena (the "Site"), which presents information about
      software products built by the operator.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Nature of the service</h2>
    <p>
      This Site is a static, informational showcase of products the operator has built. There is
      no account system, login, or in-site payment. The "Join waitlist" and "Inquire to buy"
      buttons open an email to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; any actual
      purchase or agreement is arranged separately by email. Sending an email does not by itself
      form a purchase or contract.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Product status disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      Each product shown carries one of four statuses: <code>Idea</code>, <code>Prototype</code>,
      <code>Beta</code>, or <code>Live</code>. These reflect actual development progress as
      honestly as possible and do not guarantee completion or a release date. Features, screens,
      and demo links may change or be discontinued without notice as development continues.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The Site's design, text, logo, and each product's description documents belong to the
      operator. Reproduction, redistribution, or commercial use without the operator's prior
      written consent is not permitted.
    </p>

    <h2>5. External links</h2>
    <p>
      Some product pages link to external demos or sites. The operator is not responsible for the
      content, operation, or privacy practices of those external sites.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      The Site and the information on it are provided "as is," without warranty of any kind,
      including fitness for a particular purpose or merchantability. To the fullest extent
      permitted by law, the operator is not liable for damages arising from use of the Site.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated at the operator's discretion; changes take effect once posted
      here.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: 24px 0 60px;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
</style>
